      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raju lived near a village in the Sundarbans. One evening, the smell of biryani drifted through the trees from a wedding feast. Raju followed the scent and watched the cook layer rice, meat and spices in a huge pot. He thought, \"If humans can make this, why can't I?\"\n\nThe next day, Raju gathered ingredients: rice from a farmer's field, chicken from a coop, and spices he found in a market stall. He built a fire by the river and tried to copy what he had seen. His first attempt was a disaster — burnt rice, raw chicken, too much chilli. But Raju did not give up. He practised every night, adjusting the heat, the timing, the balance of flavours.\n\nAfter many tries, Raju finally made a pot of biryani that smelled just like the wedding feast. The village animals gathered around, amazed. Even the cook from the village came to taste it and nodded in approval. Raju realised that patience and practice could turn any dream into reality, even for a tiger with paws instead of hands.\n\n6:01 AM",
